# Copy to .env and fill in what you need. Everything here is optional.
# .env is gitignored.

# ---- AWS credentials ---------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE. Listed easiest first.
#
# 1. Nothing at all. Run `aws configure` (or `aws sso login`) and these scripts use
#    whatever the AWS CLI already resolves. No long-lived keys on disk.
#
# 2. A named profile:
# AWS_PROFILE=my-personal-account
#
# 3. Explicit keys, which clear any inherited AWS_PROFILE or session token. Use
#    this when other tooling on your machine sets those and would otherwise win.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Optional. Overrides the region from your profile.
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2

# ---- Which config to deploy --------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset to deploy lib/config.ts. Point it at a gitignored copy to keep your
# server name, password, and account out of version control:
#
#   cp lib/config.ts lib/config.local.ts
#
# PALWORLD_CONFIG=lib/config.local.ts

# ---- Cloudflare (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Only if your domain is on Cloudflare and you want scripts/sync-cloudflare-ns.sh
# to write the subdomain delegation for you. Needs Zone:DNS:Edit on that zone.
# Any other registrar: run scripts/show-nameservers.sh and add them by hand.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
